  "declienting": [
    "Kept this as the governed modal-drawer structural alternate while preserving the inline-disclosure implementation as the family default; the alternate is a separate export and directory rather than a presentation prop or a second canonical.",
    "Composed the existing Modal, which owns the SSR-safe body portal, focus containment and restoration, Escape and backdrop dismissal, background inerting, scroll lock, and overlay stack; the alternate adds no competing overlay engine.",
    "Restored the source's strict 48px vertical swipe boundary: exactly 48px is below threshold, an upward movement beyond 48px opens from the mobile handle, and a downward movement beyond 48px closes from the drawer handle.",
    "Isolated dismissal swipes to the dedicated handle and left the navigation list as an independent vertical scroll region, so scrolling content cannot accidentally dismiss the drawer; named close-button and Escape alternatives remain available.",
    "Retained explicit items, ariaLabel, activeId, collapsedIcon, and expandedIcon contracts. Added only a neutral closeLabel for the shared modal close control; the portal remains document.body with no client-specific anchor.",
    "Rejected source heading scanning, sticky header-offset pinning, Sitecore editing/CMS wiring, page-content portal anchors, and scroll-close orchestration as application concerns rather than reusable component behavior.",
    "Closes the mobile dialog when the lg desktop breakpoint becomes active, keeping the hidden responsive copy unfocusable and releasing the shared overlay stack during viewport changes."
  ],
